<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Asean half year shr loss widens.</title>
<headline>Asean half year shr loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     49.4 loss   vs 3.6 loss</p>
<p>    Operating income	4.92 loss   vs 0.51 profit</p>
<p>    Tax			 nil	   vs 0.16</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.76	  vs 1.01</p>
<p>    Gross revenue	   20.86	 vs 28.29</p>
<p>    Net loss		  7.42	  vs 0.54</p>
<p>Full name: Asean Investment Corp Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     1.74 loss   vs 0.20 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Asean said the sever downturn in the textile industry had hit its results and it had spent 0.50 million rand rerstructuring the group. It warned that the firm will not return to profitability in the current financial period.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
